### Key Directories Explained

#### `/src/api/` - API Layer
- All backend communication logic
- Axios configuration with uni-app adapter
- Request/response interceptors for token and error handling
- API services organized by domain (auth, user, dictData, etc.)
- TypeScript interfaces for requests/responses

#### `/src/pages/` - Page Components
- All page-level components (views)
- Organized by feature/module (mine, work, common, etc.)
- Each page is registered in `pages.json`
- Use `index.vue` as the main page file
- Page-specific components stay in the same directory

#### `/src/components/` - Shared Components
- Reusable components used across multiple pages
- Custom components beyond @dcloudio/uni-ui
- Only move components here if truly reusable

#### `/src/store/` - State Management
- Pinia stores using setup syntax
- User store for authentication and permissions
- State persistence configured via pinia-plugin-persistedstate

#### `/src/utils/` - Utilities
- Pure utility functions
- Helpers for common operations
- Platform API wrappers
- Type checking and formatting functions

#### `/src/static/` - Static Assets
- Images, fonts, and other static files
- Accessible via relative paths in components
- Example: `@/static/images/logo.png`

### Configuration Files

- **`pages.json`** - uni-app routing configuration
  - Page paths and navigation bar settings
  - Tab bar configuration
  - Global window styles
  - easycom component auto-import rules

- **`manifest.json`** - uni-app application manifest
  - App ID, name, version
  - Platform-specific configurations
  - Permissions and capabilities

- **`vite.config.ts`** - Build tool configuration
  - Vite plugins (uni-app, TailwindCSS adapter)
  - Build options and optimizations

- **`tailwind.config.ts`** - TailwindCSS configuration
  - Custom theme settings
  - Utility class customization

- **`tsconfig.json`** - TypeScript configuration
  - Compiler options
  - Path aliases (`@/` → `src/`)
  - Type definitions

