## Development Commands
- **Dev WeChat MP**: `npm run dev:mp-weixin`
- **Dev H5**: `npm run dev:h5`
- **Build WeChat MP**: `npm run build:mp-weixin`
- **Build H5**: `npm run build:h5`
- **Type check**: `npm run type-check`
- **Other platforms**: `npm run dev:mp-{platform}` or `npm run build:mp-{platform}`

## uni-app Specifics

### Platform-Specific Code
Use conditional compilation for platform-specific features:
```vue
<!-- #ifdef H5 -->
<view>H5 specific content</view>
<!-- #endif -->

<!-- #ifdef MP-WEIXIN -->
<view>WeChat MP specific content</view>
<!-- #endif -->

<!-- #ifndef H5 -->
<view>All platforms except H5</view>
<!-- #endif -->
```

### Template Tags
- Use `<view>` instead of `<div>`
- Use `<text>` for text content
- Use `<image>` instead of `<img>`
- Use `<button>` for buttons (native component)
- Use `<input>` for text inputs (native component)

### Lifecycle Hooks
- Page lifecycle: `onLoad`, `onShow`, `onHide`, `onUnload`, `onPullDownRefresh`
- Component lifecycle: Vue 3 composition API hooks (`onMounted`, `onUnmounted`)
- Import from `@dcloudio/uni-app`:
  ```typescript
  import { onLoad, onShow, onReady } from '@dcloudio/uni-app'
  ```

## When Creating New Features

### Step-by-Step Guide

1. **Create API functions** in `/src/api/services/`
   - Follow existing patterns in Api class
   - Use TypeScript interfaces for request/response types
   - Group related APIs in services

2. **Create page component** in `/src/pages/`
   - Choose appropriate domain folder or create new one
   - Use kebab-case for folder names
   - Main page should be `index.vue`
   - Example: `/src/pages/mine/settings/index.vue`

3. **Register page** in `/src/pages.json`
   - Add page path and configuration
   - Set navigation bar title and style
   - Configure page-specific options
   - ⚠️ **CRITICAL**: The first page in the array is the entry page (app startup page)
   - ⚠️ **ALWAYS append new pages to the end** - DO NOT insert at the beginning
   - Inserting at position 0 will change the app's entry point!
   ```json
   {
     "pages": [
       {
         "path": "pages/login"  // ⚠️ DO NOT INSERT BEFORE THIS - it's the entry page!
       },
       // ... existing pages
       {
         "path": "pages/mine/settings/index",  // ✅ ADD NEW PAGES AT THE END
         "style": {
           "navigationBarTitleText": "设置"
         }
       }
     ]
   }
   ```

4. **Extract components when needed**
   - Keep page-specific components in the same directory as the page
   - Move to `/src/components/` only if truly reusable across multiple pages
   - uni-ui components are auto-imported via easycom

5. **Use TailwindCSS for styling**
   - Prefer utility classes over custom CSS
   - Use rpx units: `w-[200rpx]`, `h-[100rpx]`
   - Use responsive classes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`
   - Custom styles in `<style scoped lang="scss">` when needed

6. **Navigation**
   - Use uni API for navigation: `uni.navigateTo()`, `uni.redirectTo()`, `uni.reLaunch()`
   - Pass params via query string or global state
   - Always use absolute paths: `/pages/mine/index`

7. **Add proper TypeScript types**
   - Define interfaces for data models
   - Type all function parameters and return values
   - Use type imports from `@/api`

8. **Handle loading and errors**
   - Use `uni.showLoading()` and `uni.hideLoading()`
   - Use `uni.showToast()` for error messages
   - Implement proper try-catch blocks

9. **Test on multiple platforms**
   - Test on WeChat DevTools
   - Test on H5 (browser)
   - Test on real device when possible

10. **Follow responsive design**
    - Use rpx units for responsive sizing
    - Test on different screen sizes
    - Use TailwindCSS responsive utilities

